# PWA-S2 (#450) — Apple Pay domain verification file.
#
# Apple Pay on the Web requires this file to be served at
# `https://<domain>/.well-known/apple-developer-merchantid-domain-association`
# with HTTP 200 + a body that matches what Apple issued for the merchant ID.
#
# V1 strategy (PRD §10 PWA Client Q6, payment CONTEXT): Apple Pay domain
# verification is registered MANUALLY via the Stripe Dashboard at each Phase C
# onboarding (~2 min per tenant). Stripe acts as the merchant ID owner and
# manages the file content — when a tenant adds a custom domain, the KB Admin
# clicks « Add domain » in Stripe Dashboard and Stripe handles the per-domain
# verification under the hood (shared platform merchant ID across direct
# charges, payment CONTEXT « Apple Pay verification mutualisée »).
#
# This static file is the FALLBACK in case Stripe's automated route fails for
# a given domain. It must be replaced with the EXACT bytes Apple/Stripe issued
# for the specific merchant ID + domain pairing before the tenant goes live
# with Apple Pay. V2 automation (PRD §10 Q6): Stripe API to register the
# domain at provisioning time, no manual step.
#
# Lines starting with `#` are ignored by Apple's parser (the file is treated
# as opaque bytes), so this header is safe to ship until a real merchant ID
# is provisioned for a custom domain.
